  body: "# Employment connection of an industrial accident\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe source separates
    “arising out of” from “in the course of” employment and examines when, where and what the person was doing,
    with further enquiry sometimes needed even during normal work.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nAn event on work
    premises is not automatically an industrial accident. Employed-earner status, treated groups, excluded groups,
    territorial scope and statutory extensions must be reviewed. This source-specific test is not the same as tort
    negligence or all self-employed work.\n\n## Inspected passages\n\n- [DMG 66061, PDF page 14](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a814e8b40f0b6230269697f/dmgch66.pdf#page=14).\n\
    - [DMG 66062, PDF page 14](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a814e8b40f0b6230269697f/dmgch66.pdf#page=14).\n\
    - [DMG 66063, PDF page 14](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a814e8b40f0b6230269697f/dmgch66.pdf#page=14).\n\
    - [DMG 66301, PDF page 59](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a814e8b40f0b6230269697f/dmgch66.pdf#page=59).\n\
    - [DMG 66302, PDF page 59](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a814e8b40f0b6230269697f/dmgch66.pdf#page=59).\n\
    - [DMG 66304, PDF page 59](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a814e8b40f0b6230269697f/dmgch66.pdf#page=59).\n\
    \n## Evidence and review status\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of captured DWP guidance, not an
    official DWP document. Definitions and semantic associations are model-assisted proposals awaiting specialist
    review. No individual entitlement decision, medical conclusion, award calculation or executable rule is provided.\n\
    \nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, legal event and claimant-event dates are separate.
    Current legal applicability is unresolved. Page numbers are one-based PDF positions; machine extraction may
    damage reading order, characters and footnotes. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n- `dmg-vol11-ch66`:
    PDF `8a2f49feb6557c0bc2833c308c458204e0f28cefeabbe85bc7a1ec3ae0461155`; extracted pages `a4efac777c187bd7b7d95994b53893fc4b480fe08736216f641a27ec9d6ed3d7`;
    acquired `2026-09-15T19:45:34.019999Z`.\n"
  resource: https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a814e8b40f0b6230269697f/dmgch66.pdf#page=14
